WHAT IT IS FOR

    The audience keeps its state in DIP_SCRN's globals and in the
    arguments of fields::Get_List_Field_, and none of it is serialized:
    who is talking, whether the ambassador refused, the statement and the
    text the engine rendered for it (a random variant, so an id does not
    name the text), and the menu taking input — its menus are lists of
    equal shape. The patch records the running list's title, items and
    enable flags while Get_List_Field_ takes input (ext::ListFieldGuard)
    and appends a block, "DIPL", between INFS and COLS while 57 or 58 is
    reported. A marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 47.`, on one line at every
    changed place.

